  <p data-rte-preserve-empty="true">I returned to my snow picket and although messy as you can see but safely secured, I calmly, carefully managed the stuck rope situation. A stuck rope (or worse a lost rope here), means death.</p><p data-rte-preserve-empty="true" class="MsoNormal">Anchor by anchor I trusted my intuition, carefully checking each one and making my own when needed.   Some I backed up with threads, some I trusted solely on my own v-threading skills. I would leave material to prevent a frozen, stuck rope.&nbsp; Some of them I got to said aloud “whoever did this knew what the fuck they were doing!” One of them was a self-equalizing anchor on the same cordelette with multiple v-threads; I’d never seen that before. I made about 12 rappels, landing onto the glacier at noon exactly.</p>


  










  





















  











  
    
      
    
  
  
    
      
        
          
        
      
    
    
    



  








  
  
  




  
  
  
  
    
  



























  
    
  

    

    

    
